---
title: "v1_add (Sui Framework: deny_list)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_reserved: assert !RESERVED.contains(addr)
    q_check_reserved --> q_abort: addr is reserved
    q_abort --> [*]: abort EInvalidAddress
    q_check_reserved --> q_get_list: addr not reserved
    q_get_list --> q_check_type_exists: bag_entry = deny_list.lists[per_type_index]
    q_check_type_exists --> q_add_type: denied_addresses does not contain type
    q_add_type --> q_check_already: add(type, empty_set)
    q_check_type_exists --> q_check_already: type exists
    q_check_already --> q_return_early: addr already denied
    q_return_early --> [*]: return (no-op)
    q_check_already --> q_insert: addr not yet denied
    q_insert --> q_inc_count: denied_addresses.insert(addr)
    q_inc_count --> [*]: denied_count[addr] += 1

    note right of q_check_reserved
        INV-001: reserved system addresses cannot be denied
        INV-002: idempotent - adding already-denied address is a no-op
        INV-003: denied_count tracks cross-type deny count per address
    end note
